hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1356","Muhammad bin Bashar and Abu Musa told us, they said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, Yahya bin Saeed Al-Ansari told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, On the authority of Salih ibn Khawat, on the authority of Sahl ibn Abi Hathamah, regarding the fear prayer, he said: “The imam stands facing the Qiblah, and a group of them stands With him and a group of the enemy, their faces were towards the enemy, and he would bow with them one rak'ah."" Abu Musa said: “Then they stand up and bow,” and Bundar said: “Then they kneel for themselves, and prostrate themselves two prostrations in their place. And they go to the place of those people, and those people come and kneel with them, and prostrate with them two prostrations, so there are two for him, and they have one, Then they bow.” Abu Musa said: “One rak’ah for themselves and they prostrate two prostrations.” This is the hadith of Bundar, except for what I mentioned, which Abu Musa contradicted. In the wording of the hadith, Abu Musa only added: for themselves in the two cases only. Abu Bakr said: I heard Bandar saying: I asked Yahya about this hadith and he told me, on the authority of Shu’bah."
"1357","He said: I heard Abu Musa saying: Yahya bin Saeed told me, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Saleh bin Khawat, on the authority of Sahl bin Abi Hathamah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. Bundar said something like the hadith of Yahya bin Saeed, and Yahya said to me: Write it next to it. I do not memorize the hadith, but it is like a hadith. Yahya bin Saeed, and Abu Musa said: Yahya said to me: Did you hear from me the hadith of Yahya bin Saeed regarding the fear prayer? I said: Yes, he said: Then write it side by side like it."
